.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-30T16:27:46Z","updated_at":"2025-03-30T16:27:46Z","body":"There seems to be small inconsistency. If node is outside tree, `_notify_transform()` is called on `pos_changed`. Inside tree it's called on `approx_pos_changed` or `approx_size_changed`, so there might be edge case when the transform notify is not properly sent depending on whether node is inside or outside tree, with the same change. Not sure if it's something to worry about though 🤔\r\n\r\nAnother thing is that I wonder why `data.pos_cache = new_pos_cache;`/`data.size_cache = new_size_cache;` even need a condition, unless there is a significant performance difference in skipping the write.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2764635876/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2765190006","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104451#issuecomment-2765190006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104451","id":2765190006,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6k0XN2","user":{"login":"WinnerWind","id":71366717,"node_id":"MDQ